From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:41:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] glm cuda: EXL3 mcg experts at any whole-bit width, mixed
 by projection

Admission reads EXL3 mcg checkpoints at 1 to 8 bits: "bits" may be absent
(a mixed checkpoint gives "avg_bits"), and a given one must lie in range.
The loader takes each trellis's width from its last dimension, slices TP
shares by that width's tile bytes, places each expert's trellis at its own
offset and uploads a width table a projection (one table, as before, when
the three agree). Layer gets uniform_k2_gu and uniform_k2_d; uniform_k2
stays nonzero only when every projection agrees, so a 4-bit layer uploads
upstream's bytes and keeps the prompt kernels.

Scratch is sized by the path each layer takes: the prompt kernels' when
they take it, else the grouped path's, the buffers taking the largest over
every layer and the MTP layer (a mixed layer's prompt chunks run grouped).

